Chapter: InlineSingleCaller

 Four shapes the single-caller inliner must get
 right, run with the pass switched on by the `.flags` sidecar.

 What this test can and cannot see is worth stating, because it decides
 what it is for. A correct optimizer does not change any answer, so
 nothing below can tell whether a definition was inlined -- run it with
 the pass off and every line is identical. It is not a firing test and
 must not be read as one; that evidence is the emitted symbol map, where
 an inlined definition is absent and a declined one is present.

 What it pins is that the pass does not MISCOMPILE these four shapes,
 and the third and fourth are the pair that earns it:

   wide     a body with an `if`, which leaf inlining refuses outright, at
            a single call site.
   arity4   four parameters. Leaf inlining caps at three because it pays
            for the body at every site; a single site has nothing to
            duplicate, so the cap does not apply here.
   free     a body naming a global, inlined into a caller with no local
            of that name. Must still answer 101.
   shadowed the SAME body naming the SAME global, at a site where a local
            of that name is in scope. Splicing it there would rebind the
            global to the caller's 7 and answer 8. It must answer 101.

 `free` and `shadowed` need separate helpers with identical bodies, and
 that is not duplication for its own sake: one helper called from both
 sites would have two references, both sites would be declined for that
 reason alone, and the capture guard would never be reached. Each has to
 be a single-caller definition to put the guard under load.

 A wrong answer here is 8 on the last line. That is the capture bug this
 pass is most likely to grow, and it is the reason the pair exists.

Section: Helpers

  isc-g : Integer
  isc-g = 100

  isc-add-g : Integer -> Integer
  isc-add-g (x) = x + isc-g

  isc-add-h : Integer -> Integer
  isc-add-h (x) = x + isc-g

  isc-pick : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  isc-pick (a) (b) = if a > b then a - b else b - a

  isc-four : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  isc-four (a) (b) (c) (d) = a + b + c + d

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("wide " & show (isc-pick 9 4))
    print-line-uni ("arity4 " & show (isc-four 1 2 3 4))
    print-line-uni ("free " & show (isc-add-g 1))
    print-line-uni ("shadowed " & show (let isc-g = 7 in isc-add-h 1))
  end
